  "loop_invariants": [
    {
      "component": "encoded.atom_width",
      "invariant": "For e>=1 and profile (1,577), target=e; 1<=low<=ceil(e^(1/577))<=high<=e. Each iteration uses middle=floor((low+high)/2) and min(middle^577,target)>=target iff middle^577>=e, then high=middle or low=middle+1. The nonnegative integer high-low strictly decreases while positive; return low=high is the least w>=1 with w^577>=e."
    },
    {
      "component": "encoded.select.depth",
      "invariant": "Initially cursor=e and depth=0. Each loop with cursor>=64 sets cursor=42*floor(cursor/64) and increments depth once; this strictly contracts positive cursor. Thus depth=D(e), where D(e)=0 for e<64 and D(e)=1+D(42*floor(e/64)) otherwise. It is computed before borrowing from original, never from body or width."
    },
    {
      "component": "encoded.select.stock",
      "invariant": "For D=0 stock remains 1. Otherwise order=product_{i=0}^{63}(q^64-q^i); after j repeats level=269241600*order*q^(4096*j), j=0..w-1. After t levels stock=level^t, t=0..D. Therefore stock=(269241600*|GL_64(F_q)|*q^(4096*(w-1)))^D under the stated prime-field order identity."
    },
    {
      "component": "encoded.select.borrowing",
      "invariant": "Initially rows=1=q^0 and borrowed=0. Each iteration while rows<stock multiplies rows by q and increments borrowed. For integer q>=2 and stock>=1 it terminates at the least k>=0 with q^k>=stock; rows=q^k. Equality with stock terminates; this is covering, not strict padding."
    },
    {
      "component": "encoded.select.first_guard",
      "invariant": "body=remainder=0 initially. The first fits is exactly 2*k<e. If false, division is skipped, both zeros remain, and fits is false. If true, remaining=e-k>0, so divide receives a nonnegative numerator and positive w."
    },
    {
      "component": "encoded.select.body_guard",
      "invariant": "Only after the first guard, (body,remainder)=divmod(e-k,w); e=k+body*w+remainder and 0<=remainder<w. The final fits is body>=64. Body/remainder remain the computed values when this second guard fails. Both guards use original e and the selected w."
    },
    {
      "component": "ordinary.run/execute_plan",
      "invariant": "run passes select(original,self.q,self.profile) as the sole plan factory. execute_plan checks positive original/extents, calls that factory once, selects fitted iff plan['fits'] else fallback with original, transfers and clears the result, closes every non-fits plan value in finally, and finishes using the same fits boolean. This is a syntactic ownership/control-flow observation, not proof that the primitives discharge cleanup."
    },
    {
      "component": "profile/cohort",
      "invariant": "The default encoded Profile remains (17,10000,64,42,269241600); both opt-in retuned profile functions replace only numerator/denominator by (1,577). interface.ordinary forbids a competing profile option. retuned_native.retune checks the unchanged geometry and fresh active-cohort native; its factory reads that cohort's production.PRIME. The full active_sources AST binds its active encoded/ordinary/production references and compare_backend call; execution/cohort identity remains inherited, not activated here."
    }
  ],
